---
layout: base.njk
title: "Play an H5P activity"
description: "An H5P activity an AI chat wrote, built and played in your browser, with its .h5p file to download. Nothing is sent to a server."
# Not a page to land on from a search: it is opened with an activity's source in its link.
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
# As the build page's policy: packages it built play in the player's frame, under the policy the
# player's Service Worker gives each response there.
csp: "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src * data: blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'"
---
{#- The player alone, for an activity's source in the link (#source=, as the build page takes it),
    so that a chat app can show the activity in its reply: play-page.ts builds it and plays it. -#}
<main class="play" id="main">
  <p class="play-status" id="status" role="status" data-state="building">Building the activity in your browser…</p>
  {#- For a source that names files of the person's own, a video beside it: chosen here, where
      they stay in the browser. The field is hidden, and the button opens it. -#}
  <p class="play-files" id="files-box" hidden>
    <button type="button" class="button button-solid" id="choose">Choose the file</button>
    <input type="file" id="files" multiple hidden>
  </p>
  <div class="player-box" id="player-box" hidden>
    <h5p-player id="player"></h5p-player>
  </div>
  <p class="play-actions">
    <a class="button button-solid" id="download" download hidden>Download the .h5p</a>
    <a class="button" id="edit" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open in the build page</a>
  </p>
</main>
<script type="module" src="/h5p/play/play-page.js"></script>
